 "notes": [
  "This compares a shadow/no-shadow classification, not an illumination percentage: NASA maps the PSR as permanently shadowed, LunaNav tests whether the Sun ever clears the LOLA skyline at its centroid.",
  "Sun positions use LunaNav's analytic (Meeus) model, whose elevation agreement with Horizons is a few hundredths of a degree; the agreement margins here are degrees, so the classification is insensitive to that error.",
  "The 80 m/pix wide DEM resolves crater rims and massifs hundreds of metres across. A ridge narrower than ~80 m, or terrain beyond the ray-march, could in principle shadow a point the model calls lit, so the agreement is a lower bound on obstruction, not a polygon-wide proof.",
